---
// /benchmark/ (T134): everything this site can measure about a device, in one run and one report. It took the place
// of ?bench=1 alone, /gpu-test/ (T94) and /opfs-test/ (T137), which a visitor had to open one by one and report one
// by one. Every section runs in a worker of its own, which the page ends before the next section starts: a phone
// never holds the model, the GPU's buffers and a large file at once (T96: Chromium refused a page its third memory).
import { MODELS } from "../models.js";
// the models of the site itself: the model section loads one of them, and the line section fetches its first part
const SITE_MODELS = MODELS.filter((entry) => !entry.hf && entry.checkpoint);
// T176: the model the benchmark takes unless one is chosen: llm-jp-3 150M, heavy enough that a device's numbers mean
// something (the owner, 2026-09-27: tiny-lm is too light); ?model= still picks another
const BENCH_MODEL = "llm-jp-3-150m";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <title>Pyodide LLM · Benchmark</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 100 100%22%3E%3Ctext y=%22.9em%22 font-size=%2290%22%3E🦙%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <h1><a href="../">Pyodide LLM</a> · Benchmark</h1>
    </header>
    <main>
      <p class="intro">What this device and this browser do for the models of this site, measured in one run: the
        browser's features, the CPU, a model, the GPU, the storage and the line. Nothing is sent anywhere; at the end
        you can copy the results or open an issue with them yourself.</p>
      <div class="controls">
        <button id="run-all" type="button" class="primary">Run all</button>
        <label>model <select id="model">
          {SITE_MODELS.map((entry) => <option value={entry.id} selected={entry.id === BENCH_MODEL}>{entry.name}</option>)}
        </select></label>
        <label>storage <select id="size">
          <option value="64">64 MB</option>
          <option value="256" selected>256 MB</option>
          <option value="1024">1 GB</option>
        </select></label>
        <label><input id="large" type="checkbox" /> GPU: also Llama 3.2 3B (3.2 GB)</label>
        <label><input id="full" type="checkbox" /> model: every step (slower)</label>
      </div>
      <p id="overall" class="overall" hidden></p>
      <section data-section="device">
        <h2>This browser</h2>
        <p class="about">WebAssembly SIMD and relaxed SIMD, 64-bit memories, shared memory (software threads), WebGPU and
          the private file system, as the model page finds them.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-section="cpu">
        <h2>CPU</h2>
        <p class="about">The model page's own forward pass on a made-up int8 model as wide as Llama 3.2 1B (211 MB of
          weights a token), with 1, 2, 4 and on software threads, doubling up to the logical cores. Beside it, the CPU's
          ceilings: how fast it reads alone, and loops of int8 dots and of float multiply-adds.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-section="model">
        <h2>Model</h2>
        <p class="about">The chosen model, with and without the SIMD kernels: the table of "Measure this browser" on the
          model page. Without the kernels the weights take four times the memory; a browser that does not say how much
          memory the device has (Safari, Firefox) skips that round, and its row says so.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-section="gpu">
        <h2>GPU</h2>
        <p class="about">WebGPU: the adapter, its shaders checked against JavaScript, how fast it reads int8 weights, and
          a token's work of three model sizes against the CPU. Then the same token with the next token chosen on the GPU,
          one layer of a token as separate steps and fused into fewer dispatches, where that layer's time goes step
          by step, tokens generated on the GPU (the
          sampling too) each read back as it comes or several at once, what a token costs besides its
          weights, the device's ceilings (loops of multiply-adds, int8 dots or reads alone), and a prompt's tokens all
          at once, with the share of its ceiling each shader reaches. The weights are random bytes.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-section="storage">
        <h2>Storage</h2>
        <p class="about">The browser's private file system: a file written 8 MB at a time, in order and far apart, then
          read back and checked. The file is removed at the end.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-section="line">
        <h2>Line</h2>
        <p class="about">A part of this site's model and a range of a model on huggingface.co: the wait for the first byte
          and the speed. Then huggingface.co read no faster than 1, 4 and 8 MB/s, as a slower line would deliver it.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-section="memory">
        <h2>Page memory</h2>
        <p class="about">How much memory this page can hold before the browser refuses it or ends the tab (an iPhone ends
          a tab past about 2 to 3 GB, with no error). Not part of Run all: run it on its own, after you have reported or
          copied the other sections' results (a tab that is ended loses them). Keep this page in front until it ends:
          hiding it (another app, the screen locked) or leaving it stops the run. The tab may be reloaded, and the page
          then says how far it got.</p>
      </section>
      <div class="report" hidden>
        <h2>Results</h2>
        <p><button id="copy" type="button">Copy the results</button> <a id="issue" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Report them as an issue</a>
          <span id="long" class="about" hidden>(long: the issue gets a summary, and the whole results go to your clipboard: paste them into the issue)</span>
          <span id="longer" class="about" hidden>(too long even for a summary: the issue gets only a request for the results, and the whole results go to your clipboard: paste them into the issue)</span></p>
        <p id="clipboard" role="status" hidden>This browser did not let the page write to your clipboard. The whole
          results are in the box below, and the page tried to select them: copy them by hand (on a phone, a long press on
          the text may bring up Copy) and paste them into the issue.</p>
        <pre id="markdown"></pre>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff; --panel: #f4f4f5; --text: #18181b; --muted: #71717a; --line: #e4e4e7;
    --accent: #2563eb; --accent-text: #ffffff; --bad: #dc2626;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", "Hiragino Sans", "Noto Sans JP", sans-serif;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg: #0f0f11; --panel: #1c1c1f; --text: #ededf0; --muted: #9a9aa3; --line: #2c2c31; --accent: #3b82f6; --bad: #f87171; }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }
  header, main { max-width: 792px; margin-inline: auto; padding: 10px 16px; }
  header { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  h1 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; }
  h1 a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  h2 { font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .intro, .about { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 4px 0 8px; }
  .controls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 8px 0 16px; }
  button, select { font: inherit; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text); background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; }
  button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: default; }
  button.primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-text); border-color: var(--accent); }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 12px 0; }
  .head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .head .state { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  /* T177: a running section's stage and how long it has run, so that a long one is not taken for a frozen page */
  .overall { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: -8px 0 12px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .progress { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 4px 12px; align-items: baseline; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 8px 0 2px; }
  .progress[hidden] { display: none; }
  .progress .bar { grid-column: 1 / -1; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--line); overflow: hidden; }
  .progress .bar > div { height: 100%; width: 0; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--accent); transition: width 0.3s; }
  /* no count of stages: a piece going back and forth */
  .progress .bar.unknown > div { width: 30%; animation: sweep 1.6s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
  @keyframes sweep { from { margin-left: 0; } to { margin-left: 70%; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .progress .bar.unknown > div { animation: none; width: 100%; opacity: 0.35; } }
  .progress .stage { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .progress .elapsed { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .state.ok { color: inherit; }
  .state.wrong, .state.error { color: var(--bad); }
  #clipboard { color: var(--bad); font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 4px 0 8px; }
  /* a table wider than a phone scrolls inside itself: the page never does */
  .out { overflow-x: auto; }
  .out table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.8rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin: 6px 0; }
  .out th, .out td { text-align: left; padding: 3px 12px 3px 0; vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; }
  /* a table of two columns (a name and its value: "This browser") wraps its words instead (T186: at 360 px the
     storage's value was cut off on the right) */
  .out table.pairs th, .out table.pairs td { white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word; }
  .out th { font-weight: 500; color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .out p { font-size: 0.8rem; margin: 4px 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: 0.75rem; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px; }
</style>

<script>
  // T353: the script is the modules of src/benchmark/, read here in the order their statements ran as one script: dom.ts
  // (the elements, the URL, the sections' names), isolation.ts (the service worker and its one reload: what follows
  // waits for it), state.ts (what the parts share), section.ts (what a section runs on: its progress, its worker), a
  // module a section or two (cpu.ts, model.ts, gpu.ts, storage.ts, memory.ts), report.ts and run.ts (the Run buttons,
  // the run, ?run=).
  import "../benchmark/dom.ts";
  import "../benchmark/isolation.ts";
  import "../benchmark/state.ts";
  import "../benchmark/section.ts";
  import "../benchmark/cpu.ts";
  import "../benchmark/model.ts";
  import "../benchmark/gpu.ts";
  import "../benchmark/storage.ts";
  import "../benchmark/memory.ts";
  import "../benchmark/report.ts";
  import "../benchmark/run.ts";
</script>
